WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
New students move onto one floor, each with their own catchphrase.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.200
A term later?

3
00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:17.328
Each picks up what most neighbours say, and dialect zones grow by themselves.

4
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:20.410
This is label propagation.

5
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:26.543
One rule: join the label with the largest total weight among your neighbours.

6
00:00:26.543 --> 00:00:31.343
At the start, each node's label is its own name.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.578
Round 1 goes A to E in turn. A switches to B.

8
00:00:41.578 --> 00:00:45.978
C's turn: add up the weights per label.

9
00:00:45.978 --> 00:00:50.556
B = 5, D = 2, E = 1: C takes B.

10
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.780
D switches to E; E keeps E.

11
00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.380
Round 1 ends: three nodes changed.

12
00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.780
ABC | DE has already formed.

13
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:06.617
Round 2: every node votes again.

14
00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:11.017
Nothing changed, and only that counts as stable.

15
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:14.017
Two rounds, cut 3.

16
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.160
What if everyone changes at once?

17
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.160
A copies B, B copies A —

18
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:33.133
Swap over, swap back: it never stops.

19
00:01:33.133 --> 00:01:36.822
That is a cycle, not convergence.

20
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:48.411
Visit E to A instead: 3 rounds, other label names, the same groups.

21
00:01:48.411 --> 00:01:54.767
Raise C–D to 10: the groups become AB | CDE, cut 5.

22
00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:59.122
Same rule; turn a knob, and the answer changes.

23
00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:03.403
On G01, try all 120 visiting orders:

24
00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:09.537
The groups are always ABC | DE; only the rounds vary, 2 or 3.

25
00:02:09.537 --> 00:02:13.737
This small graph is steady; bigger ones may not be.

26
00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:20.360
A 24-cell circuit: the same rule finds 3 blocks, cut 2.

27
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:27.500
One local rule, with no need to say how many groups,

28
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:33.500
and the circles appear on their own.

29
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:40.500
But the order, the update mode and the tie rule all change it.

30
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:48.500
Next module: a number for every point.

31
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.600
In the lab below, step through every vote.
